      "text": "This problem involves solving a system of simultaneous equations. We can represent the total value of the coins in the jar with a formula: ( text{total_value} = text{value_nickels} cdot text{num_nickels} + text{value_dimes} cdot text{num_dimes} + text{value_quarters} cdot text{num_quarters} ). Since we know that the amount of quarters is (frac{text{num_quarters}}{3}), we can replace (text{num_implies_{quarters}}) with (frac{text{num_nickels} + text{num_dimes}}{3}). Substituting, we get ( text{total_value} = text{value_nickels} cdot text{num_nickels} + text{value_dimes} cdot frac{text{num_implies_{quarters}} cdot text{num_nickels} + text{value_dimes} cdot text{num_dimes}}{3} + text{value_quarters} cdot frac{text{num_nickels} + text{num_dimes}}{3} ). Rearranging, we get ( text{total_value} = frac{text{value_nickels} cdot text{num_nickels} text{value_dimes} cdot text{num_nickels} + text{value_dimes} cdot text{num_dimes} + 2 cdot text{value_quarters} cdot text{num_nickels} + 2 cdot text{value_quarters} cdot text{num_dimes}}{3} ) or further ( text{total_value} cdot 3 = text{value_nickels} cdot text{num_nickels} text{value_dimes} cdot text{num_nickels} + text{value_dimes} cdot text{num_dimes} + 2 cdot text{value_quarters} cdot text{num_nickels} + 2 cdot text{value_quarters} cdot text{num_dimes} ). Simplifying, ( text{total_value} cdot 3 = text{value_nickels} cdot text{num_nickels} (text{num_nickels} + text{num_dimes} + 2) ). Thus, ( text{num_nickels} = frac{text{total_value} cdot 3}{text{value_nickels} (text{num_nickels} + text{num_dimes} + 2) + text{value_dimes} cdot text{num_dimes} + text{value_quarters} cdot 2} ).\n\nResult:\nThe total number of coins in the jar is ( frac{text{total_value} cdot 3 - text{value_dimes} cdot text{num_dimes} - text{value_quarters} cdot 2}{text{value_nickels} (text{num_nickels} + text{num_dimes} + 2) + text{value_dimes} cdot text{num_dimes}} ). \n\nTo find the number of nickels ( (text{num_nickels}) ) and dollars ( (text{num_dimes}) ), we further simplify and solve (text{total_value} = text{value_nickels} cdot 5 cdot text{num_nickels} + text{value_dimes} cdot 10 cdot text{num_dimes} + text{value_quarters} cdot 25 cdot text{num_quarters}) into expressions similarly, resulting in knowing exact values of all coins. This computation can be encapsulated within the program as:\n\n```python\ndef calculate_nickels(dollars,num_dimes):\n    \"\"\"\n    This function calculates the number of nickels equal to the number of dimes.\n    \n    Parameters:\n    dollars (int): The total value of the coins in cents.\n    num_dimes (int): The number of dimes.\n    \n    Returns:\n    int: The number of nickels.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    # Calculate the number of quarters\n    num_quarters = (dollars - (5*num_dimes) - (2*num_dimes*2)) / (25*2)\n    \n    # Calculate the total value of nickels, dimes and quarters\n    total_value = 5*num_dimes + 10*num_dimes + 25*num_quarters\n    \n    # Calculate the number of nickels\n    num_nickels = (dollar_value * 3 - num_dimes * 10 - 2 * num_quarters * 2) / (num_nickels + num_dimes + 2)\n    \n    return int(num_nickels)\n```\n\nSo the rationale is: Knowing the number of dimes, calculate the total value of dimes and quarters, compute the remaining cents for nickels, divide these by (5 + 10 + 50) to get the number of nickels.\n\nThe answer is (text{num_nickels}).",
