      "text": "Let x be the number of nickels, dimes, and quarters.\nThe value of each nickel is 0.05 dollars, dimes is 0.10 dollars and quarters is 0.25 dollars. So the problem in forming an equation would be:\n0.05x + 0.10x + 0.25x = 13.20\nSolving for x:\n.40x = 13.20\nx = 13.20/.40 = 33\nThe fewest number of Nickels Jamie has in his jar is 33\nWeegy: The fewest number of Nickel was 33. (More)QuestionExpert VerifiedAnswerExpert(Physics, Chemistry, Biology, 766949) SalvationalUser: Thanks for saving my life The fewest number of Baseball cards must have been _____?\nAlgebra and corresponding graphing (766949) SalvationalUser: Thanks for saving my life Each week Newton throws 3 hardballs and 5 softballs. If he played in 15 weeks in all how many total number of baseball did he throw?\nSolution:\nSince he played 15 weeks in all, which mean he will throw 15 times 3 hardballs and 15 times 5 softballs. So to get the sum of the number of hardballs and softballs he will throw in 15wks.\nSo x= 15*3 and y=15*5\nx+ y= 45 + 75= 120 total number of balls he will throw each week.\nThis problem could be represented with the following equation:\nLet x be the total number of baseball cards, which mean Newton must have 15x baseball cards.\nSince each week he had 3 hardballs then after 15 wks, the total number of baseball she throws is 15(3)=45. 5 softballs means she will throw 15(5)=75. Together it will be 45+75=120.\nThe answer is 120 balls (More)QuestionExpert VerifiedAnswerExpert(Physics, Chemistry, Biology, 766949) SalvationalUser: Thanks for saving my life In Nigeria how much the year budget?\nAlgebra and corresponding graphing (766949) SalvationalUser: Thanks\"\nThanks for saving my life\"\"(More)\nQuestionExpert VerifiedAnswerExpert(Physics, Chemistry, Biology, 766949) SalvationalUser: Re: Thanks\"\" Re: Thanks\"\nThanks for saving my life Kentucky football cornerback Diamond Brice sticks his head up in the huddle to prepare for a snap against Florida | Football | Southeaster