      "text": "Let $n$ represent the number of nickels, dimes, and quarters.\nThe value of the nickels is $0.05n$.\nThe value of the dimes is $0.10n$.\nThe value of the quarters is $0.25n$.\nThe total value of the coins is $0.05n + 0.10n + 0.25n = 0.40n$.\nWe know that the total value of the coins is $13.20, so we set up the equation $0.40n = 13.20$.\nDividing both sides of the equation by $0.40$, we find that $n = \\frac{13.20}{0.40} = 33$.\nTherefore, Jamie has $\\boxed{33}$ nickels. The answer is: 33",
